    crm:P67i_is_referred_to_by [ a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
            crm:P190_has_symbolic_content "Circular or rectangular flat dishes, generally made of wood, pottery or metal, on which meat or other food is carved or served. Early wooden examples often have a depressed area for food and a second smaller cavity for salt. Use \"chargers\" for large platters, usually circular or oval and often made of earthenware or metal, used for serving meat. [Source: Getty AAT]" ;
